Z||000000||2farnorth||06-03-2001||08:14 AM||||I have an 85 2.5, 5 speed that has had an acceleration lag ever since I bought it.   After going through all the sensors and the distributor without making any difference, I started playing with the timing.  At 8 degrees it would lag until it got to about 3000 rpm and then accelerate good.  I advance the timing to about 15 advanced  and the the acceleration improved a lot.  I then brought it up to about 20 degrees and it ran just a little better, so I left it there.  It's not binding the starter so I think I've got a problem either in the timing gear or the balancer pulley.  Anyone got any ideas?<P>thanks<BR>Dave||||reg||5
Z||000001||SteveJ||06-03-2001||08:53 AM||||Take a 1/4 wooden dowel to feel the top of the piston through the spark plug hole and rotate the engine by hand until number one cylinder is at top dead center. (some people use a Bic pen) Then look at your timing marks to see what they read. Seems to me I have read numerous reports here on the board of harmonic balancers shifting position.||||reg||1
